---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Software and release status
description: Explore ForgeWire Labs software, public sources, screenshots, release status, and current project boundaries.
permalink: /projects/index.html
---
<section class="page-lead page-shell" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">ForgeWire Labs · Software</p>
  <h1 id="projects-title">Independent software, with <em>its own purpose and release state.</em></h1>
  <p class="lead-copy">The projects make different contributions to the organization's engineering work. Each keeps its own source, architecture, availability, and limits. This is a portfolio of separate systems, not a single released platform.</p>
  <p class="lead-index"><span>Released software</span><span>Previews</span><span>Private development</span></p>
</section>

<section class="repository-spread page-shell" aria-labelledby="repopact-title">
  <div class="spread-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">ForgeWire Labs · Repository systems</p>
    <h2 id="repopact-title">RepoPact</h2>
    <p>Core defines and validates governed repository state. Workbench is a separate native interface that consumes Core and carries its own preview status.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="repo-product-grid">
    {% for project in projects %}{% if project.id == "repopact-core" or project.id == "repopact-workbench" %}
      <article class="product-entry product-entry--{{ project.statusKind }}" data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
        <div class="product-entry-top"><span>{{ project.kicker }}</span><span class="status status--{{ project.statusKind }}">{{ project.status }}</span></div>
        <h3><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3>
        <p>{{ project.summary }}</p>
        <p class="availability-copy"><strong>Availability.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
        <div class="product-entry-links"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% if project.secondaryUrl %}<a href="{{ project.secondaryUrl }}">{{ project.secondaryAction }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% endif %}</div>
      </article>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="repo-evidence-grid">
    <figure class="architecture-figure architecture-figure--page">
      <img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg" alt="RepoPact Core architecture: repository records connect to a canonical Rust engine, which serves CLI and Workbench clients and produces evidence and derived views. An optional host or CI integration has a provider-specific boundary." aria-describedby="repopact-diagram-notes" width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>RepoPact Core architecture from its <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core/blob/614689b127cf52f801877cc48440f7e45c3709eb/docs/assets/readme/repopact-architecture.svg">public architecture documentation</a>.</figcaption>
      <p class="diagram-notes" id="repopact-diagram-notes"><strong>Diagram key.</strong> Blue arrows show exchanges with the Core engine; slate arrows show people, host integrations, evidence, and derived views; dashed boxes mark derived views. The host/CI box is optional and provider-specific. <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg">Open the full-size diagram</a>.</p>
    </figure>
    <figure class="screenshot-figure">
      <div class="screenshot-focus screenshot-frame--light"><img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/workbench-desktop-dashboard.jpg" alt="RepoPact Workbench desktop capture focused on its repository validation summary. The capture was made from a Windows x64 source build." width="1362" height="930" loading="lazy"></div>
      <figcaption><strong>RepoPact Workbench · Source-build preview.</strong> The README documents this genuine Windows x64 capture as a local build using a disposable Core conformance fixture. The visible counts are fixture data, not customer, production, or reliability metrics. Packaged installers are not listed. <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/workbench-desktop-dashboard.jpg">Open the full-resolution capture</a> · <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-workbench/blob/414a4a78091796735a1b97b03fd8c3cf1c105f30/docs/assets/readme/workbench-desktop-dashboard.jpg">View its source and provenance ↗</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="private-section" aria-labelledby="private-title">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <div class="private-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research and private development</p>
      <h2 id="private-title">Work can be architecturally important before it is available.</h2>
      <p>The public materials describe direction and status. No public build or supported deployment is available for these projects.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="private-register">
      {% for project in projects %}{% if project.group == "private" %}
        <article class="private-record" data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
          <p class="eyebrow">{{ project.kicker }}</p>
          <h3>{% if project.url %}<a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% else %}{{ project.name }}{% endif %}</h3>
          <p>{{ project.summary }}</p>
          <p class="availability-copy"><strong>{{ project.status }}.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
          {% if project.url %}<a class="text-link" href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% endif %}
        </article>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="planning-spread page-shell" aria-labelledby="anvil-title">
  <div class="planning-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">ForgeWire Labs · Planning</p>
  </div>
  {% for project in projects %}{% if project.id == "anvil" %}
    <article class="planning-entry" data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
      <div class="product-entry-top"><span>{{ project.kicker }}</span><span class="status status--{{ project.statusKind }}">{{ project.status }}</span></div>
      <h2 id="anvil-title"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h2>
      <p class="planning-summary">{{ project.summary }}</p>
      <p class="availability-copy"><strong>Boundary.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}
</section>

<section class="communication-section" aria-labelledby="flink-title">
  <div class="page-shell communication-layout">
    <div class="communication-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">ForgeWire Labs · Communications</p>
      {% for project in projects %}{% if project.id == "flink" %}
        <div data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
          <div class="product-entry-top"><span>{{ project.kicker }}</span><span class="status status--{{ project.statusKind }}">{{ project.status }}</span></div>
          <h2 id="flink-title"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h2>
          <p>{{ project.summary }}</p>
          <p class="availability-copy"><strong>Ownership and release.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
          <div class="product-entry-links"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="{{ project.secondaryUrl }}">{{ project.secondaryAction }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </div>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <figure class="flink-figure">
      <img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/flink-product-architecture.svg" alt="Flink's documented product model shows a human operator, communication cockpit, governed API and MCP boundary, providers as channel edges, and ForgeWire or Fabric as optional integration edges." aria-describedby="flink-diagram-notes" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>Adapted from Flink’s public product-model diagram; its source predates the repository rename and the latest release materials retain the former ForgeLink name. Dashed edges describe optional integrations, not proof that an integration is implemented. <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/flink-product-architecture.svg">Open the full-size diagram</a>.</figcaption>
      <p class="diagram-notes" id="flink-diagram-notes">The diagram labels solid lines as Flink ownership and dashed lines as optional edges. It describes Flink only; it does not imply a shared architecture across ForgeWire Labs projects.</p>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="learning-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="skillforge-title">
  <div class="learning-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">Learning software · <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/skillforge-command-center.png">Open full-size screenshot</a></p>
    {% for project in projects %}{% if project.id == "skillforge-academy" %}
      <div data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
        <div class="product-entry-top"><span>{{ project.kicker }}</span><span class="status status--{{ project.statusKind }}">{{ project.status }}</span></div>
        <h2 id="skillforge-title"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h2>
        <p>{{ project.summary }}</p>
        <p class="availability-copy"><strong>Release boundary.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
        <div class="product-entry-links"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="{{ project.secondaryUrl }}">{{ project.secondaryAction }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <figure class="learning-shot">
    <div class="screenshot-frame screenshot-frame--dark"><img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/skillforge-command-center.png" alt="SkillForge Academy command center with course navigation, a recommended study drill, progress panels, and domain coverage." width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy"></div>
    <figcaption>Screenshot used in the public organization profile and captured from the published Windows app. The displayed 0% values and practice counts are sample account state, not learner outcome metrics. Newer course-platform beta surfaces are not shown. <a href="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/skillforge-command-center.png">Open the full-resolution image</a>.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section class="ownership-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="ownership-title">
  <div class="section-heading section-heading--stacked">
    <p class="eyebrow">Software index</p>
    <h2 id="ownership-title">Current scope and availability</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Release state describes the linked project's public evidence at the time of this review. It does not imply support beyond the source project's own terms.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="table-scroll-hint" id="ownership-table-hint">On a narrow screen, swipe horizontally to see all three columns. Keyboard users can focus this table region and use the arrow keys to scroll.</p>
  <div class="ownership-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Software scope and maturity table" aria-describedby="ownership-table-hint">
    <table class="ownership-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Project</th><th scope="col">Public scope</th><th scope="col">Current limit</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core">RepoPact Core</a><span class="status status--released">Released CLI · 3.1.3</span></th><td>Repository state, validation, schemas, and typed operations.</td><td>The stable package is version-scoped; the source branch may be newer.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-workbench">RepoPact Workbench</a><span class="status status--preview">Source-build preview</span></th><td>Native presentation and application orchestration for supported Core operations.</td><td>No packaged installer is listed. Recorded platform checks do not establish universal support.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/anvil">Anvil</a><span class="status status--preview">Developer preview</span></th><td>Local planning records and typed links to external work.</td><td>Single-writer JSON store; API and schema can change; no execution or audit-trail ownership.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/Flink">Flink · ForgeWire Labs</a><span class="status status--released">Latest package · v2.0.1</span></th><td>Local communication state and human coordination.</td><td>Repository version 2.0.3; published release materials retain the former ForgeLink name.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/skillforge-academy">SkillForge Academy</a><span class="status status--released">Windows app · 1.3.2</span></th><td>Published offline-first certification learning application.</td><td>Newer course-platform work has a separate beta status.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/ForgeWire-Overview">ForgeWire</a><span class="status status--private">Private development</span></th><td>Application and runtime direction for configured models, tools, project context, and selected workflows around work a person can review.</td><td>The overview distinguishes current paths from active architecture work. No public application build or supported install path.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/ForgeWire-Overview/blob/85d1905b0bd8db420882f00065daff34833dab27/README.md#3-fabric-dispatch-and-remote-execution">Fabric · ForgeWire Labs</a><span class="status status--private">Private development</span></th><td>Separate control-plane direction for authenticated, policy-gated work across machines.</td><td>Limited, configuration-dependent integration for selected ForgeWire workflows; broader integration and release gates remain open. Not a public service.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="source-note">The source notes identify the reviewed repository revisions and image provenance.</p>
</section>

<section class="availability-foot page-shell" aria-labelledby="availability-title">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow">Status guide</p>
    <h2 id="availability-title">Availability means what the source says.</h2>
  </div>
  <ul>
    <li><span class="status status--released">Released</span><span>A package or application is available through the linked release channel. The repository's current branch may be newer.</span></li>
    <li><span class="status status--preview">Preview</span><span>Source or early software is available to inspect; packaging, API, schema, or platform support can still change.</span></li>
    <li><span class="status status--private">Private development</span><span>Public overview material may exist, but there is no public build or release to install.</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p class="source-note">Product links and maturity notes were checked against the linked public repositories and release pages. Preview and source-build status carries no production-support claim.</p>
</section>
